  { q: "Is it normal to understand English but not speak it?", a: "Yes. It's the usual state for adult learners, especially anyone who learned mostly by reading and listening. Recognition always outruns production; the gap is expected rather than a sign you learned wrong." },
  { q: "How do I go from understanding English to speaking it?", a: "Shift your time from input to output. Speak short answers daily, get corrected on the exact words you got wrong, rehearse the specific conversations you're avoiding, and track one measurable thing, like pronunciation scores on the same words each week." },
  { q: "How long does it take to start speaking fluently?", a: "It depends on how much you produce each day rather than how many months you're enrolled. There's no honest fixed timeline, and anyone promising one is selling something." },
